Step 1: Understand what GCD means
GCD is the largest number that divides both numbers exactly.
Example:
12 and 18
Common divisors: 1, 2, 3, 6
Greatest = 6

Step 2: Notice the pattern (Euclidean Algorithm)
Instead of checking every number, use this observation:
GCD(a, b) = GCD(b, a % b)
Keep replacing:
a with b
b with a % b
Until b becomes 0.
Example: 48 and 18

a	  b	  a % b
48	18   12
18	12	  6
12  6	    0
When b = 0, answer is a = 6.

class Solution {
    public int findGCD(int[] nums) {
        int a = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        int b = Integer.MAX_VALUE;

        for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++){
            a = Math.max(a,nums[i]);
            b = Math.min(b,nums[i]);

        }
        while(b!=0){
            int mod = a%b;
            a = b;
            b = mod;
        }

        return a;


        
    }
}
